Package: nexus-base-files
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, base-files
Description: NEXUS OS identity and base system files
 Identifies the installed system as NEXUS OS: os-release, login banners and
 the distribution description used by system tools and the NEXUS desktop.
 .
 The files Debian's base-files package owns are diverted rather than
 replaced, so Debian point-release updates of base-files keep applying
 cleanly.

Package: nexus-boot
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
 grub-common, grub2-common, efibootmgr, os-prober, mokutil,
 shim-signed,
 grub-efi-amd64-signed | grub-efi-arm64-signed,
 grub-efi-amd64-bin | grub-efi-arm64-bin
Recommends: grub-pc-bin
Conflicts: grub-pc, grub-efi-amd64, grub-efi-arm64, grub-efi-ia32, grub-coreboot, grub-ieee1275, grub-xen
Description: NEXUS OS boot loader management
 Keeps the GRUB boot loader of an installed NEXUS OS system current.
 .
 NEXUS OS starts through Debian's Microsoft-signed shim and Debian-signed
 GRUB so that UEFI Secure Boot works without enrolling keys. This package
 provides nexus-grub-install, which copies those signed binaries onto the EFI
 System Partition (or writes the legacy BIOS boot sector), maintains the
 "NEXUS OS" firmware boot entry, and is re-run automatically by a dpkg
 trigger whenever a GRUB or shim security update is installed. It replaces
 the grub-pc/grub-efi-* front-end packages and ships the GRUB defaults.

Package: nexus-installer
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3 (>= 3.11),
 nexus-boot,
 parted, gdisk, fdisk, util-linux, dosfstools, e2fsprogs, squashfs-tools,
 cryptsetup, cryptsetup-initramfs, lvm2, initramfs-tools, udev, passwd, locales,
 console-setup, apt
Description: NEXUS OS installer engine
 The non-interactive engine that installs NEXUS OS from the live medium to
 disk. It probes the machine, turns an answer file into an explicit plan
 (every partition created, formatted or kept), and carries out a plan only
 when given the hash of the plan that was shown.
 .
 Supports whole-disk installation, installation into free space alongside
 other operating systems, and manual partition assignment; GPT, UEFI with
 Secure Boot, legacy BIOS on amd64, and LUKS2 full-disk encryption. The
 graphical installer and unattended installations both drive this engine.

Package: nexus-live
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, live-boot, live-boot-initramfs-tools, live-config, live-config-systemd,
 live-tools, user-setup, sudo
Description: NEXUS OS live-session configuration
 Configures the system for running from the installation medium: the live
 user account, host name and session start-up. It is removed from the
 installed system by the installer.

Package: nexus-archive-keyring
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: OpenPGP key and APT source of the NEXUS OS package repository
 The public key that authenticates the NEXUS OS package repository (NEXUS
 CORE, SECURITY and COMMUNITY) and the APT source entry for it.
 .
 The source entry is enabled only in builds that were given a repository URL;
 otherwise it is installed disabled, so the system never points at a
 repository that does not exist.

Package: nexus-hardening
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3, nftables, apparmor, auditd, sudo, iproute2, init-system-helpers,
 util-linux, procps
Recommends: apparmor-profiles, apparmor-profiles-extra, apparmor-utils, cryptsetup-bin, mokutil,
 nexus-boot
Description: NEXUS OS security baseline
 The security configuration NEXUS OS ships with, as one removable package:
 .
  * kernel hardening through sysctl and kernel command-line parameters;
  * no implicit loading of rarely used network protocol and filesystem
    modules;
  * a default-deny nftables host firewall and nexus-firewall to manage it;
  * audit rules for identity, privilege, kernel-module and boot-chain changes;
  * NetworkManager privacy defaults (per-network MAC address, IPv6 privacy);
  * nexus-security-status, the read-only JSON report of firewall, AppArmor,
    disk encryption, Secure Boot, updates, listening services, logins, audit
    and hardening state that the Security Center displays.
 .
 Every setting is documented with what it protects against and what it can
 affect; none of them disables a security mechanism to make software work.

Package: nexus-artwork
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: NEXUS OS wallpapers and logos
 The original NEXUS OS artwork: the default wallpapers (Horizon, Lattice,
 Aurora and Daylight) and the NEXUS logo family in SVG.

Package: nexus-ui
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends},
 qml6-module-qtquick, qml6-module-qtquick-controls, qml6-module-qtquick-layouts,
 qml6-module-qtquick-window, qml6-module-qtquick-templates, qml6-module-qtquick-effects,
 qml6-module-qtquick-dialogs, qml6-module-qtquick-shapes, qml6-module-qtqml-models,
 qml6-module-qtqml-workerscript, qml6-module-qtcore, qml6-module-qtqml,
 qt6-svg-plugins, qt6-wayland,
 fonts-inter-variable, fonts-jetbrains-mono
Recommends: qt6-image-formats-plugins
Description: NEXUS user-interface library (NexusUI)
 The shared foundation of the NEXUS HORIZON desktop and every NEXUS
 application: the design tokens as a QML theme, the NEXUS Qt Quick Controls
 style, the NexusUI component set and the symbolic icon set.

Package: nexus-horizon
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends},
 nexus-ui (= ${binary:Version}), nexus-artwork,
 kwin-wayland, xwayland, kwin-style-breeze, qml6-module-org-kde-layershell,
 plasma-integration, breeze-icon-theme, breeze-cursor-theme, hicolor-icon-theme,
 libkf6service-bin, kio6,
 dbus-user-session, polkitd, pkexec,
 xdg-desktop-portal, xdg-desktop-portal-kde, xdg-user-dirs, xdg-utils,
 shared-mime-info, desktop-file-utils
Recommends: xdg-desktop-portal-gtk, sddm, pipewire, pipewire-pulse, wireplumber,
 network-manager, bluez, upower, power-profiles-daemon, udisks2, accountsservice
Description: NEXUS HORIZON desktop shell and session
 The desktop of NEXUS OS: top panel, dock, application launcher, wallpaper,
 session menu and the polkit authentication dialog, running as a Wayland
 session on the KWin compositor. Also provides the "NEXUS HORIZON" entry for
 the login screen and the compositor defaults.

Package: nexus-sysinfo
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, nexus-ui (= ${binary:Version}),
 util-linux, pciutils
Description: NEXUS System Information
 Shows operating system and kernel versions, firmware, processor, memory,
 graphics, storage and virtualisation, read from the running system.
